{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffyAnXE5HVm1d1DsQSzW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate, `rule_built_tally_switch_triplet`, and the self-check printed `OK`. Its ELPD-LOO on the short check fit was −3409.8, against −3435.5 for the incumbent and −3437.2 for the model I refined. Treat that number with caution: it came from a single 100-draw fit, and PSIS-LOO flagged 11.8% of trials as unreliable. Admission's full fit decides. The check did not test novelty against the other models, convergence or the 30-minute fit limit.\n\n**What I refined:** `tally_span_switch_ideal_triplet_variety`, the model statistically tied with the incumbent. I kept its tally span, ideal switching rate, three-flip chunk variety and personal left/right lean.\n\n**The one change:** a single shared penalty on sequences built by a visible construction rule. A sequence counts if either:\n- a short unit is copied throughout (HTHTHTHT, HHTHHT), or\n- it reads the same backwards with heads and tails swapped (HHHTHTTT, HHHHTTTT).\n\n**Why this change:** I checked which pairs the refined model predicts worst, then tried adding single candidate features to its fit. Each feature got one weight, fitted against the model's own posterior samples; this is a rough in-sample screen.\n- The two kinds of rule penalised separately gained about 8.5 nats each. Counted as one \"rule-built\" flag they gained 16.6, so they behave like one mechanism.\n- The backwards-swapped symmetry also still gained about 3 nats on the incumbent, which already penalises copied units. That makes it the part this candidate adds beyond the incumbent.\n- The symmetric sequences are not periodic and their chunk variety is ordinary, so neither the incumbent nor the triplet model catches them. That fits the critique that people's choices on some pairs are more one-sided than predicted, although that critique did not survive the FDR correction (q = 0.29).\n\nOne other feature scored about as well in the screen (+9.3): whether a sequence starts and ends on the same face. I left it out because I couldn't give it a clear psychological reading.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_5`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":78391,"cache_read_input_tokens":11602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":78391,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d796bca4-1c97-43ea-83c3-e1a12d91f825","uuid":"48ca4c9e-d18c-441e-a2ef-5ba03a772463","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:54:44.275Z","request_id":"req_011CffyAmt36zExu2exqWFwn"}
